# Stakeholder List, Map, or Personas (BABOK® Technique)

## What This Technique Is

This technique identifies and analyzes **stakeholders impacted by or influencing an initiative**, and may represent them as:
- Lists
- Influence/interest maps
- Personas

---

## Why This Technique Exists

Projects fail when key stakeholders are:
- Missed
- Not engaged
- Engaged incorrectly

BABOK includes this technique to ensure **right engagement, at the right time**.

---

## When to Use

- Project initiation
- Stakeholder engagement planning
- Change management
- Risk and impact analysis

---

## How Stakeholders Are Analyzed

- Influence vs interest
- Power vs impact
- Needs, concerns, expectations
- Communication preferences

---

## Real-World Example (Banking / IT)

Identifying stakeholders for a payments platform:
- Ops (high interest)
- Compliance (high influence)
- IT (high impact)
- Customers (external)

---

## Common Mistakes

- Stakeholder list created once and forgotten
- No prioritization of engagement
- Ignoring indirect stakeholders

---

## Key Takeaway

Effective stakeholder analysis enables **targeted communication and smoother delivery**.
